course: dictionary
lesson: 6104
title: Sound words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are sounds. Writers use them to make a story come alive, so you can hear the animal. «Miaou» is the sound a cat makes, so when you read it, you can almost hear the cat.
explain: Miaou is a sound word, called onomatopoeia. The word sounds like the thing it describes. Context helps here too: «The cat miaoued at the door» tells you that a cat is making a sound, and that miaoued is a verb, an action word.
explain: Animals sound different in different languages. In French, cats say «miaou» too, but dogs say «ouaf ouaf» and cows say «meuh». Spellings change as well: «miaow» is common in the UK, and «meow» in the USA.
fact: Onomatopoeia is a word that sounds like the sound it describes.
fact: «Miaou» means the sound a cat makes.
fact: As a verb, «miaou» means to make the sound of a cat, and it can change: miaoued, miaouing.
fact: «Miaow» is the common spelling in the UK, and «meow» is common in the USA.
fact: In French, animal noises include «ouaf ouaf» (woof woof), «meuh» (moo) and «coin-coin» (quack quack).
exercise: «The cat miaoued at the door.» What does miaoued mean? | Came in through the window | Slept on the mat | *Made the sound a cat makes | Ran out of the house
exercise: Which French word is the sound a cow makes? | ouaf | *meuh | miaou | coin-coin
exercise: Which spelling would you most likely see in the USA? | ouaf | miaou | miaow | *meow
test: Which word is a noun meaning a cat's cry? | *a miaou | miaous! | miaoued | miaouing
test: What does «miaou!» mean? | *A cat's cry | A dog's bark | A hen's cluck | A cow's moo
exam: Ella reads, «The kitten miaouing loudly woke the baby.» What is the kitten doing? | *Making a cat's cry, loudly | Chasing a ball | Sleeping soundly | Drinking milk
